# Headers for files served by Workers Static Assets, which answer before the
# Worker runs. Responses the Worker produces get theirs in workers/security-headers.ts.
# The policy applies when a file is opened on its own, not when a page loads it.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Every file under /assets/ is written by Vite with a hash of its content in its
# name, so a file at one address never changes: the browser keeps it for a year
# and never asks again. Without this, each page load revalidated every script,
# stylesheet and font (about 60 requests), and the stylesheet's round trip held
# back the first paint. Everything else here (the icons, the manifest, the
# images) keeps its name across deploys and is still revalidated. Pages and
# their .data answers come from the Worker and stay `private, no-store`
# (workers/no-copy.ts). docs/decisions.md, "Placement and caching".
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
